        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0293" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/1675: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-19T11:00:00+08:00">October 19,
                            1939—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 19—7:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>French official circles here comment on growing Soviet influence in China, the
                    heavy increase in Soviet military supplies for Chinese forces, renewed activity
                    of Soviet airmen who are said to have carried out the recent raids over Hankow,
                    and heavy augmentation of staff of Soviet Embassy including numerous military
                    advisers. At the same time it is reported here that the French military mission
                    is leaving China, and I learn confidentially that “some” of the French troops in
                    China “may be” withdrawn for service in France.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
